; Invalid: `:feedback true` on the LAST `(pass …)` of a `(pass-graph …)`. The
; last pass renders to the canvas, and WebGPU keeps no previous canvas texture
; to read, so there is nothing for `prev_trail` to be. The hook used to lower
; it anyway (a pooled rgba8unorm target under a canvas-format pipeline — a GPU
; validation error and a black canvas). Feed back in an earlier pass and let
; the last one read it: `textureLoad(<name>, …)` / `textureSample(<name>, samp, uv)`.

(pass-graph
  (pass :name trail :feedback true :code """
    @fragment fn fs(@builtin(position) pos: vec4f) -> @location(0) vec4f {
      return textureLoad(prev_trail, vec2i(pos.xy), 0) * 0.98;
    }
  """))
